# Orientation
##Repository
- The repository root is accessibility-audit-api-docs/ — the folder containing
.github/ , docs/ , and README.md . Every path in this plan (e.g.
docs/spec/openapi.yaml ) is relative to it.
- VS Code: New File icon + full path (e.g. docs/spec/openapi.yaml ) creates missing
folders automatically.
- Cmd+S saves — an unsaved file is invisible to Git and every tool
below.
- Dot files ( .gitignore , .vale.ini ) are normal, just hidden in Finder.

## Commands:
Terminal: opens at the repo root.
- pwd confirms where you are
- ls -a lists everything including dot files.

### Git loop

1. **In Terminal:**
git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b docs/notes-vocabulary # new branch; name describes the work
# ...create and edit files, save...
git add docs/notes/api-vocabulary.md
git commit -m "Add plain-English API vocabulary notes"
git push -u origin docs/notes-vocabulary

2. **On GitHub:**
Compare & pull request → Create pull request → (checks pass, once CI
exists in Phase 6) → Merge.

**Back in the terminal:**
git checkout main && git pull .